A||||12||la9||Front License plate Holder||||5||
Z||000000||la9||03-26-2000||05:20 PM||||I have an 86 SE and it has no place for the front license plate. Is it supposed to ? I've only found one Fiero picture with a license plate on the front and if I put one there it would block the holes for air-flow to my radiator. The only choice I see right now is to drill holes in the front fascia. Either way sounds like a bad deal to me. I wouldn't worry about it but everyone says it is against the law not to have a front plate in Ohio. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||03-26-2000||06:06 PM||||Fiero's in states that required front plates had brakets on them.... The plate holder just bolts onto the front fascia... so if you drill a couple holes, it won't be any different.  If you want to take a look, mine has a front plate on it, although its an 88 Formula and has a slightly different front Fascia... your 896 SE would have essentially the same setup however.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/index.htm</A> <BR>click on 88 Fiero Pics at the top.<P>I have 2 pics that show the front plate.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||03-26-2000||06:38 PM||||I have never looked closely at the aero front fascias, but I am pretty sure there are holes for a plate braket. <BR>Just so you don't feel overly concerened, I have been driving my Fiero here in Ohio for over a year(around 14,000 miles) without a front plate. I don't like the way it looks on there, so I left it off. No problems yet. Never know, could get stopped any day.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||03-26-2000||07:33 PM||||Well, if you want one, I have a license plate holder of off my 86 GT that I am not using. I live in Oklahoma where they don't even give ou a front plate, so I don't need it anymore. <BR>  Basically, the thing clamps on to the opening in the nose from behind.  It does pull the nose into weird shapes, but my cars nose found it's original shape after a while.<BR>  As far as the airflow, I don't think it makes a huge difference<BR>as most of the air coming to the radiator comes from under the car.<BR>  Well, if you want it, let me know. One of these days I will actually get down to Mailboxes Etc. and ship off some stuff thatpeople have asked me for.  Honestly!||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||03-26-2000||08:59 PM||||I'm in Cali, and you must have a front plate. I think the Fiero Store sales the bracket, but DO NOT drill the front fascia, please don't!!! Take a look: <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=15436465&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=15436465&Sequence=2</A> <P>It mounts Just as Stimpy said. It clamps to the inside upper and lower lip/inside edge.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||03-26-2000||11:06 PM||||Just took mine off of the Grape Ape.  Gave it to a friend.  No holes.  But it did scrape some of the paint off where the corners were.||||reg||1
Z||000006||la9||03-26-2000||11:21 PM||||Hey Fiero56. It is a law. I called the Highway Patrol and asked nicely. Unfortunatly it didn't end that way. I asked if it was OK if I left the front plate on the dash until I figured out what to do. He gave me the standard response of not understanding how someone could have such contempt for the law. So I called him a few choice words and hung up. I ended up grabbing a bracket off of a corsica and drilling one hole in the fascia and bolting it on under the passenger's side turn signal. Which probably doesn't meet Ohio code either. I'd keep driving without it but I'd rather not spend the night in jail after expressing my outlaw ways to an officer that lives in the perfect world.||||reg||1
Z||000007||doughboySE||03-26-2000||11:40 PM||||JUST MY 2 CENTS I LIVE IN CANADA AND I DONT HAVE A PLATE ON THE FRONT THOUGH I SHOULD HAVE.<BR>WHAT I DO IS I USE THOSE REALLY SMALL BUNGGY CORDS THEY SELL AT CRAPPY TIRE I MEAN THE REALLY SMALL ONES AND I HAVE MY PLATE ATTACHED TO MY PASSENGER SIDE SUNVISSOR . THAT WAY IF IM AT A CAR SHOW OR PARKED CLEANING IT I FLIP IT UP AND IF I CRUZ WHERE I KNOW THERE ARE COPS AROUND I JUST FLIP IT DOWN. ACTUALLY LOOKS COOL OUTSIDE THE CAR TO||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||03-27-2000||12:13 AM||||  How much restriction does the front license<BR>plate cause on air flow for  engine cooling purposes? in the past I have had periods of overheating even though all else seemed well.<BR> could it be that my front plate is causing that kind of airflow restriction? Keep in mind this only happens on extremely hot Vegas summer days.<P>  Thanx, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000009||la9||03-27-2000||12:17 AM||||Police said it must be mounted to the front bumper. Ohio cops are real picky in Ohio especially about speeding. Either that or they just have it in for me. Probably the fact I drive at least 110 miles a day.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dan86gt3.8||03-27-2000||05:23 AM||||Yall ask shaun what he does??? Hes a fellow ohio'ian.  Here in texas the require one, but the onyl time you get messes with is the highway patroll, for some reason they just don't apreciate a nce clean looking fascia.  I have seen some fbodys screw them onto the air damn, they get tore up, but I guess its one way around it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||03-27-2000||08:54 AM||||While reading a Miata forum once, one of the guys gave his answer for a hidden plate. He put it under the front fascia, and attached it on hinges. The plate is spring loaded to spring out if a cop is seen. The guy ran a wire up into the cabin, and the cable when pulled tight and attached to a post, holds the plate flat under the fascia, unseen. But if a cop is seen, he unwinds the wire, and the plate pops out. <P>The cops here in the Dayton area might be a little different than where you live. They never even look twice at me. Dad didn't want to drill holes in his car for a front plate and has left it off for two years with no problem. But like I said before, doesn't mean I won't be pulled over today on my way to class(hope not).||||reg||1
Z||000012||BENGAL4||03-27-2000||11:50 AM||||56, I don't think the Dayton cops will bother you. You just have to watch out for the small town cops. I was pulled over in a town called St. Louisville, for not having a front plate. These guys arent even cops. They are constables. They have to call the sheriff to arrest somebody. After my ticket, this guy watched me everytime I came into town. I played in a softball league there, so I would tie it to the front facsia with shoestrings whenever I had to go there. This guy was like Henrich Himmler.||||reg||13
